.TH WHEATLEY 1 "July 2026" "Quant 1.0.0" "Quant Language Tools"
.SH NAME
wheatley \- static linter for the Quant language
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B wheatley
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] [\fIFILE\fR ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B wheatley
analyses Quant source files (\fI.qa\fR) for style violations, suspicious
patterns, and correctness issues that the type checker does not report.
It operates purely on the parsed and type-checked AST without executing
code.
.PP
Diagnostics are printed to stdout in the format:
.PP
.RS
\fIfile\fR:\fIline\fR:\fIcol\fR: [\fIW\fR|\fIE\fR] \fImessage\fR
.RE
.PP
where \fBW\fR is a warning and \fBE\fR is an error. Errors cause
.B wheatley
to exit with status 1.
.PP
.B wheatley
is also integrated into the Language Server Protocol via
.BR quant\-lsp (1):
its diagnostics appear alongside type errors in supporting editors without
a separate invocation.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-fix
Automatically fix violations that have a safe, mechanical correction
(e.g. removing an unused variable declaration). Unfixable warnings are
still reported.
.TP
.B \-\-deny \fIRULE\fR
Treat the named rule as an error instead of a warning. May be given
multiple times.
.TP
.B \-\-allow \fIRULE\fR
Suppress the named rule entirely. May be given multiple times.
.TP
.B \-\-rules
Print a list of all available rule names and exit.
.SH RULES
.TP
.B unused\-var
A variable is declared but never read. (Warning)
.TP
.B unused\-param
A function parameter is never used in the body. (Warning)
.TP
.B unreachable\-code
Statements appear after a \fBreturn\fR in the same block. (Warning)
.TP
.B missing\-return
A non-void function can reach the end of its body without a
\fBreturn\fR statement on all paths. (Error)
.TP
.B fn\-naming
Function names must be \fIsnake_case\fR. (Warning)
.TP
.B type\-naming
Struct and error-set names must be \fIPascalCase\fR. (Warning)
.TP
.B empty\-block
An \fBif\fR or \fBwhile\fR body contains no statements. (Warning)
.TP
.B shadow
A local variable hides a variable of the same name in an outer scope. (Warning)
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
No errors found (warnings may still be present).
.TP
.B 1
At least one error-level diagnostic was emitted, or a file could not be parsed.
.SH EXAMPLES
Lint a whole project:
.PP
.RS
.B wheatley src/*.qa
.RE
.PP
Treat naming violations as errors in CI:
.PP
.RS
.B wheatley \-\-deny fn\-naming \-\-deny type\-naming src/*.qa
.RE
.PP
Auto-fix what can be fixed:
.PP
.RS
.B wheatley \-\-fix src/main.qa
.RE
.SH NOTES
The name
.B wheatley
is a reference to the Aperture Science personality core of the same name
from the Portal series.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR glados (1),
.BR quant\-fmt (1),
